msgid "Quit Zed"
msgstr "Quit ForgeKairos"

msgctxt "menu"
msgid "Zed"
msgstr "ForgeKairos"

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "(Linux only) whether Zed or your compositor should draw window decorations."
msgstr "(Linux only) whether ForgeKairos or your compositor should draw window decorations."

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "Command to automatically run when Zed creates a Terminal Thread shell in the agent panel. Runs in your configured shell."
msgstr "Command to automatically run when ForgeKairos creates a Terminal Thread shell in the agent panel. Runs in your configured shell."

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "Disable all Git integration features in Zed."
msgstr "Disable all Git integration features in ForgeKairos."

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "Expose Zed itself as an IDE server on 127.0.0.1 so the Claude Code CLI in the integrated terminal and external agents can read the open files, selections and diagnostics. Diffs can be accepted or rejected in an editor tab. Makes no outgoing connections. Disabled by default."
msgstr "Expose ForgeKairos itself as an IDE server on 127.0.0.1 so the Claude Code CLI in the integrated terminal and external agents can read the open files, selections and diagnostics. Diffs can be accepted or rejected in an editor tab. Makes no outgoing connections. Disabled by default."

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "Files or globs of files that will be excluded by Zed entirely. They will be skipped during file scans, file searches, and not be displayed in the project file tree. Takes precedence over \"File Scan Inclusions\""
msgstr "Files or globs of files that will be excluded by ForgeKairos entirely. They will be skipped during file scans, file searches, and not be displayed in the project file tree. Takes precedence over \"File Scan Inclusions\""

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "Files or globs of files that will be included by Zed, even when ignored by git. This is useful for files that are not tracked by git, but are still important to your project. Note that globs that are overly broad can slow down Zed's file scanning. \"File Scan Exclusions\" takes precedence over these inclusions"
msgstr "Files or globs of files that will be included by ForgeKairos, even when ignored by git. This is useful for files that are not tracked by git, but are still important to your project. Note that globs that are overly broad can slow down ForgeKairos's file scanning. \"File Scan Exclusions\" takes precedence over these inclusions"

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "Hand the shells of SSH terminals to the remote Zed server. Running commands keep going when the connection drops, and reconnecting shows the output so far again so you can carry on. Closing the tab ends the shell. Not available on Windows remote hosts."
msgstr "Hand the shells of SSH terminals to the remote ForgeKairos server. Running commands keep going when the connection drops, and reconnecting shows the output so far again so you can carry on. Closing the tab ends the shell. Not available on Windows remote hosts."

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "Optimize Zed's interface for assistive technology such as screen readers. When enabled, otherwise-collapsed controls stay expanded and keyboard-reachable."
msgstr "Optimize ForgeKairos's interface for assistive technology such as screen readers. When enabled, otherwise-collapsed controls stay expanded and keyboard-reachable."

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "Send anonymized usage data like what languages you're using Zed with."
msgstr "Send anonymized usage data like what languages you're using ForgeKairos with."

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "The custom set of icons Zed will associate with files and directories."
msgstr "The custom set of icons ForgeKairos will associate with files and directories."

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "The folder log files are written to (`~` is expanded). When empty, logs are saved to `terminal-sessions` in Zed's log folder."
msgstr "The folder log files are written to (`~` is expanded). When empty, logs are saved to `terminal-sessions` in ForgeKairos's log folder."

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "The language of Zed's menus, settings and messages. Some text, such as tab titles, switches after a restart."
msgstr "The language of ForgeKairos's menus, settings and messages. Some text, such as tab titles, switches after a restart."

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "Use LSP tasks over Zed language extension tasks."
msgstr "Use LSP tasks over ForgeKairos language extension tasks."

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "What to restore from the previous session when opening Zed."
msgstr "What to restore from the previous session when opening ForgeKairos."

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "When opening Zed, avoid Restricted Mode by auto-trusting all projects, enabling use of all features without having to give permission to each new project."
msgstr "When opening ForgeKairos, avoid Restricted Mode by auto-trusting all projects, enabling use of all features without having to give permission to each new project."

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "Whether breakpoints should be reused across Zed sessions."
msgstr "Whether breakpoints should be reused across ForgeKairos sessions."

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "Whether to automatically surround text with characters for you. For example, when you select text and type '(', Zed will automatically surround text with ()."
msgstr "Whether to automatically surround text with characters for you. For example, when you select text and type '(', ForgeKairos will automatically surround text with ()."

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "Whether to automatically type closing characters for you. For example, when you type '(', Zed will automatically add a closing ')' at the correct position."
msgstr "Whether to automatically type closing characters for you. For example, when you type '(', ForgeKairos will automatically add a closing ')' at the correct position."

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "Whether to disable all AI features in Zed."
msgstr "Whether to disable all AI features in ForgeKairos."

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "Whether to log messages between active debug adapters and Zed."
msgstr "Whether to log messages between active debug adapters and ForgeKairos."

msgctxt "settings"
msgid "Which settings should be activated only in Preview build of Zed."
msgstr "Which settings should be activated only in Preview build of ForgeKairos."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Apply profile settings on top of Zed's default settings, ignoring user customizations."
msgstr "Apply profile settings on top of ForgeKairos's default settings, ignoring user customizations."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Command to automatically run when Zed creates a Terminal Thread shell in the agent panel.\nThe command is sent to the shell as if typed, so it is interpreted by your\nconfigured shell (including on Windows and remote/WSL projects).\nAn empty string disables this behavior.\n\nDefault: \"\""
msgstr "Command to automatically run when ForgeKairos creates a Terminal Thread shell in the agent panel.\nThe command is sent to the shell as if typed, so it is interpreted by your\nconfigured shell (including on Windows and remote/WSL projects).\nAn empty string disables this behavior.\n\nDefault: \"\""

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Configuration for developer-oriented instrumentation tools that collect\ndiagnostic data about a running Zed instance."
msgstr "Configuration for developer-oriented instrumentation tools that collect\ndiagnostic data about a running ForgeKairos instance."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Configuration of audio in Zed."
msgstr "Configuration of audio in ForgeKairos."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Configuration of the terminal in Zed."
msgstr "Configuration of the terminal in ForgeKairos."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Configuration of voice calls in Zed."
msgstr "Configuration of voice calls in ForgeKairos."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Configures what draws Zed's window decorations on Linux.\nThis setting has no effect on other platforms."
msgstr "Configures what draws ForgeKairos's window decorations on Linux.\nThis setting has no effect on other platforms."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Controls previous session restoration in freshly launched Zed instance.\nValues: empty_tab, last_workspace, last_session, launchpad\nDefault: last_session"
msgstr "Controls previous session restoration in freshly launched ForgeKairos instance.\nValues: empty_tab, last_workspace, last_session, launchpad\nDefault: last_session"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Controls whether Zed or the window manager or compositor draws window decorations on Linux.\n\nDefault: client"
msgstr "Controls whether ForgeKairos or the window manager or compositor draws window decorations on Linux.\n\nDefault: client"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Directory subtrees that sandboxed terminal commands may always write\nto without prompting. Each entry is either a bare path string or an\nobject `{requested, resolved}`; Zed writes objects (the canonical,\nsymlink-resolved target established at approval time), while\nhand-authored entries may be bare path strings. Paths written by Zed\nare absolute.\nDefault: []"
msgstr "Directory subtrees that sandboxed terminal commands may always write\nto without prompting. Each entry is either a bare path string or an\nobject `{requested, resolved}`; ForgeKairos writes objects (the canonical,\nsymlink-resolved target established at approval time), while\nhand-authored entries may be bare path strings. Paths written by ForgeKairos\nare absolute.\nDefault: []"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Directory the log files are written to. `~` is expanded.\nWhen empty, logs go to Zed's log directory under `terminal-sessions`.\n\nDefault: \"\""
msgstr "Directory the log files are written to. `~` is expanded.\nWhen empty, logs go to ForgeKairos's log directory under `terminal-sessions`.\n\nDefault: \"\""

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Format code using Zed's Prettier integration."
msgstr "Format code using ForgeKairos's Prettier integration."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Format files using Zed's Prettier integration (if applicable),\nor falling back to formatting via language server."
msgstr "Format files using ForgeKairos's Prettier integration (if applicable),\nor falling back to formatting via language server."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "If enabled, Zed will download its own copy of Node."
msgstr "If enabled, ForgeKairos will download its own copy of Node."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "If the server supports sending tasks over LSP extensions,\nthis setting can be used to enable or disable them in Zed.\nDefault: true"
msgstr "If the server supports sending tasks over LSP extensions,\nthis setting can be used to enable or disable them in ForgeKairos.\nDefault: true"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Open directories as a new workspace in the current Zed window's sidebar."
msgstr "Open directories as a new workspace in the current ForgeKairos window's sidebar."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Open projects in the current Zed window."
msgstr "Open projects in the current ForgeKairos window."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Per-tool permission rules for granular control over which tool actions\nrequire confirmation.\n\nThe global `default` applies when no tool-specific rules match.\nFor external agent servers (e.g. Claude Agent) that define their own\npermission modes, \"deny\" and \"confirm\" still take precedence — the\nexternal agent's permission system is only used when Zed would allow\nthe action. Per-tool regex patterns (`always_allow`, `always_deny`,\n`always_confirm`) match against the tool's text input (command, path,\nURL, etc.)."
msgstr "Per-tool permission rules for granular control over which tool actions\nrequire confirmation.\n\nThe global `default` applies when no tool-specific rules match.\nFor external agent servers (e.g. Claude Agent) that define their own\npermission modes, \"deny\" and \"confirm\" still take precedence — the\nexternal agent's permission system is only used when ForgeKairos would allow\nthe action. Per-tool regex patterns (`always_allow`, `always_deny`,\n`always_confirm`) match against the tool's text input (command, path,\nURL, etc.)."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Restore all workspaces that were open when quitting Zed."
msgstr "Restore all workspaces that were open when quitting ForgeKairos."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Send anonymized usage data like what languages you're using Zed with.\n\nDefault: true"
msgstr "Send anonymized usage data like what languages you're using ForgeKairos with.\n\nDefault: true"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Settings for using LSP pull diagnostics mechanism in Zed."
msgstr "Settings for using LSP pull diagnostics mechanism in ForgeKairos."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Settings related to Vim mode in Zed."
msgstr "Settings related to Vim mode in ForgeKairos."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "The URL used as the key for credential storage.\n\nWhen set, credentials are stored under this URL instead of `server_url`.\nThis allows running multiple Zed instances side by side without them\noverwriting each other's keychain entries."
msgstr "The URL used as the key for credential storage.\n\nWhen set, credentials are stored under this URL instead of `server_url`.\nThis allows running multiple ForgeKairos instances side by side without them\noverwriting each other's keychain entries."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "The extensions that should be automatically installed by Zed.\n\nThis is used to make functionality provided by extensions (e.g., language support)\navailable out-of-the-box.\n\nDefault: {}"
msgstr "The extensions that should be automatically installed by ForgeKairos.\n\nThis is used to make functionality provided by extensions (e.g., language support)\navailable out-of-the-box.\n\nDefault: {}"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "The layout of window control buttons in the title bar (Linux only).\n\nThis can be set to \"platform_default\" to follow the system configuration, or\n\"standard\" to use Zed's built-in layout. For custom layouts, use a\nGNOME-style layout string like \"close:minimize,maximize\".\n\nDefault: \"platform_default\""
msgstr "The layout of window control buttons in the title bar (Linux only).\n\nThis can be set to \"platform_default\" to follow the system configuration, or\n\"standard\" to use ForgeKairos's built-in layout. For custom layouts, use a\nGNOME-style layout string like \"close:minimize,maximize\".\n\nDefault: \"platform_default\""

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "The model's name in Zed's UI, such as in the model selector dropdown menu in the agent panel."
msgstr "The model's name in ForgeKairos's UI, such as in the model selector dropdown menu in the agent panel."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "The model's name in Zed's UI, such as in the model selector dropdown menu in the assistant panel."
msgstr "The model's name in ForgeKairos's UI, such as in the model selector dropdown menu in the assistant panel."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "The name of the Zed theme to use."
msgstr "The name of the ForgeKairos theme to use."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "The path to the npm binary Zed should use (defaults to `.path/../npm`)."
msgstr "The path to the npm binary ForgeKairos should use (defaults to `.path/../npm`)."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "This base keymap settings adjusts the default keybindings in Zed to be similar\nto other common code editors. By default, Zed's keymap closely follows VSCode's\nkeymap, with minor adjustments, this corresponds to the \"VSCode\" setting.\n\nDefault: VSCode"
msgstr "This base keymap settings adjusts the default keybindings in ForgeKairos to be similar\nto other common code editors. By default, ForgeKairos's keymap closely follows VSCode's\nkeymap, with minor adjustments, this corresponds to the \"VSCode\" setting.\n\nDefault: VSCode"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Use LSP tasks over Zed language extension ones.\nIf no LSP tasks are returned due to error/timeout or regular execution,\nZed language extension tasks will be used instead.\n\nOther Zed tasks will still be shown:\n* Zed task from either of the task config file\n* Zed task from history (e.g. one-off task was spawned before)"
msgstr "Use LSP tasks over ForgeKairos language extension ones.\nIf no LSP tasks are returned due to error/timeout or regular execution,\nForgeKairos language extension tasks will be used instead.\n\nOther ForgeKairos tasks will still be shown:\n* ForgeKairos task from either of the task config file\n* ForgeKairos task from history (e.g. one-off task was spawned before)"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Use only the files Zed had indexed"
msgstr "Use only the files ForgeKairos had indexed"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "What base settings to start from before applying this profile's overrides.\n\n- `user`: Apply on top of user's settings (default)\n- `default`: Apply on top of Zed's default settings, ignoring user customizations"
msgstr "What base settings to start from before applying this profile's overrides.\n\n- `user`: Apply on top of user's settings (default)\n- `default`: Apply on top of ForgeKairos's default settings, ignoring user customizations"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Whether the breakpoints should be reused across Zed sessions.\n\nDefault: true"
msgstr "Whether the breakpoints should be reused across ForgeKairos sessions.\n\nDefault: true"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Whether to automatically surround text with characters for you. For example,\nwhen you select text and type '(', Zed will automatically surround text with ().\n\nDefault: true"
msgstr "Whether to automatically surround text with characters for you. For example,\nwhen you select text and type '(', ForgeKairos will automatically surround text with ().\n\nDefault: true"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Whether to automatically type closing characters for you. For example,\nwhen you type '(', Zed will automatically add a closing ')' at the correct position.\n\nDefault: true"
msgstr "Whether to automatically type closing characters for you. For example,\nwhen you type '(', ForgeKairos will automatically add a closing ')' at the correct position.\n\nDefault: true"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Whether to build dev container images with BuildKit.\n\nWhen unset, Zed auto-detects BuildKit by probing for the `buildx` CLI\nplugin. Set to `false` to force the classic Docker builder, which is\nrequired for Docker-compatible engines that lack an integrated BuildKit\n(e.g. Apple Container via a Docker-API bridge), where BuildKit builds\ncannot resolve locally-built images.\n\nDefault: null (auto-detect)"
msgstr "Whether to build dev container images with BuildKit.\n\nWhen unset, ForgeKairos auto-detects BuildKit by probing for the `buildx` CLI\nplugin. Set to `false` to force the classic Docker builder, which is\nrequired for Docker-compatible engines that lack an integrated BuildKit\n(e.g. Apple Container via a Docker-API bridge), where BuildKit builds\ncannot resolve locally-built images.\n\nDefault: null (auto-detect)"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Whether to disable all AI features in Zed.\n\nDefault: false"
msgstr "Whether to disable all AI features in ForgeKairos.\n\nDefault: false"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Whether to expose this window over the loopback IDE server, so that\nexternal agents such as the Claude Code CLI can read the open editors,\nthe selection and the diagnostics, and show diffs inside Zed.\n\nDefault: false"
msgstr "Whether to expose this window over the loopback IDE server, so that\nexternal agents such as the Claude Code CLI can read the open editors,\nthe selection and the diagnostics, and show diffs inside ForgeKairos.\n\nDefault: false"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Whether to give agents Zed's IDE tools (the `zed` MCP server: highlights,\nannotations, code tours, hover, definitions, references and symbol\nsearch), in the Claude Code CLI tabs and in external agents' sessions\nalike. Independent of `enabled`: the server starts for them on demand\nand writes no lock file unless `enabled` is on.\n\nDefault: true"
msgstr "Whether to give agents ForgeKairos's IDE tools (the `zed` MCP server: highlights,\nannotations, code tours, hover, definitions, references and symbol\nsearch), in the Claude Code CLI tabs and in external agents' sessions\nalike. Independent of `enabled`: the server starts for them on demand\nand writes no lock file unless `enabled` is on.\n\nDefault: true"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Whether to log messages between active debug adapters and Zed\n\nDefault: true"
msgstr "Whether to log messages between active debug adapters and ForgeKairos\n\nDefault: true"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Whether to optimize Zed's interface for assistive technology such as\nscreen readers.\n\nDefault: false"
msgstr "Whether to optimize ForgeKairos's interface for assistive technology such as\nscreen readers.\n\nDefault: false"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Whether to run agent terminal commands outside the OS sandbox, with\nZed's own permissions (the inverse of the settings UI's \"enable sandbox\"\nswitch). When true, the sandboxed terminal tool is not exposed and the\nsystem prompt omits the sandbox section, so the model uses the plain\n`terminal` tool; on Windows, WSL sandbox setup is skipped. Such commands\nare never auto-approved: each one asks first. Only the user sets this;\nthe agent has no way to ask for a command to run outside the sandbox.\nDefault: false"
msgstr "Whether to run agent terminal commands outside the OS sandbox, with\nForgeKairos's own permissions (the inverse of the settings UI's \"enable sandbox\"\nswitch). When true, the sandboxed terminal tool is not exposed and the\nsystem prompt omits the sandbox section, so the model uses the plain\n`terminal` tool; on Windows, WSL sandbox setup is skipped. Such commands\nare never auto-approved: each one asks first. Only the user sets this;\nthe agent has no way to ask for a command to run outside the sandbox.\nDefault: false"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Whether to use gitignored files when searching.\nOnly the file Zed had indexed will be used, not necessary all the gitignored files.\n\nDefault: Smart"
msgstr "Whether to use gitignored files when searching.\nOnly the file ForgeKairos had indexed will be used, not necessary all the gitignored files.\n\nDefault: Smart"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Whether to use the system provided dialogs for Open and Save As.\nWhen set to false, Zed will use the built-in keyboard-first pickers.\n\nDefault: true"
msgstr "Whether to use the system provided dialogs for Open and Save As.\nWhen set to false, ForgeKairos will use the built-in keyboard-first pickers.\n\nDefault: true"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Whether to use the system provided prompts.\nWhen set to false, Zed will use the built-in prompts.\nNote that this setting has no effect on Linux, where Zed will always\nuse the built-in prompts.\n\nDefault: true"
msgstr "Whether to use the system provided prompts.\nWhen set to false, ForgeKairos will use the built-in prompts.\nNote that this setting has no effect on Linux, where ForgeKairos will always\nuse the built-in prompts.\n\nDefault: true"

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Zed draws its own window decorations/titlebar (client-side decoration)."
msgstr "ForgeKairos draws its own window decorations/titlebar (client-side decoration)."

msgctxt "settings schema"
msgid "Zed's Prettier integration settings.\nAllows to enable/disable formatting with Prettier\nand configure default Prettier, used when no project-level Prettier installation is found.\n\nDefault: off"
msgstr "ForgeKairos's Prettier integration settings.\nAllows to enable/disable formatting with Prettier\nand configure default Prettier, used when no project-level Prettier installation is found.\n\nDefault: off"

msgctxt "wsl sandbox step"
msgid "checking Zed's data folder"
msgstr "checking ForgeKairos's data folder"
